{"kind":"finding","id":"FN-B-truth-phone-tracker-components-2-a-01","date":"2026-11-25","lens":"2","surface":"phone","area":"phone/tracker-components-2","refs":["F-phone-802"],"severity":"S4","title":"A weight logged in pounds can show as a long, odd kilo number in the set box","what":"Pounds are stored as the exact kilos (135 lb is about 61.23496995 kg). When the member uses kilos, the weight box writes the stored number out in full with no rounding, so a set first logged in pounds (on the phone before a switch to kilos, from the watch, or from a pounds import) ticks into the box as something like 61.23496995, while the grey hint above it said 61.23.","expected":"The box shows the same tidy number as the hint and every other screen (at most two decimals in kilos), while the exact value stays stored.","evidence":["apps/mobile/src/tracker/components/unitText.ts:72-77","apps/mobile/src/tracker/components/unitText.ts:62-70","apps/mobile/src/tracker/services/restDone.ts:64-68","apps/mobile/src/tracker/components/SetRow.tsx:159","apps/mobile/src/tracker/components/SetRow.tsx:177-182","apps/mobile/src/tracker/components/setRowLayout.ts:166-174"],"proof":"code-read","root_cause_key":"metric-weight-box-not-rounded","who":"members who switch pounds to kilos or import pounds","how_often":"each time such a set is shown in a box","fix_line":"Round the kilo box text to two decimals the same way the hint does, keeping the stored value exact","fix_size":"small","needs_him":false,"verified":"pending","status":"open"}
